  "description": "1. Competition Launch & Registrations (21st–27th November) The competition will officially be launched on 21st November. Registrations will remain open until 27th November, 11:50 PM. 2. Round 1 – Online Quiz (28th November–1st December) All registered teams will participate in an online quiz round. The quiz round will remain open for four days, from 28th November to 1st December. The quiz submissions will then be evaluated, and shortlisted teams will qualify for the next round. 3. Round 2 – Case Study Submission (3rd–10th December) Shortlisted teams will receive a case study on 3rd December. Teams will have until 10th December, 11:59 PM, to analyse the case and submit their solutions. The submission will be in the form of an executive summary presented through a PowerPoint deck. The submissions will undergo a two-day evaluation process to shortlist the finalists. 4. Round 3 – Final Jury Presentation (14th–15th December) The shortlisted finalists will present their case solutions before the jury on 14th and 15th December. The jury will evaluate the presentations, assess the proposed solutions, and determine the winners. Jury & Evaluation: We are planning to have two jury members from Product Folks, who will evaluate the finalist teams during the final presentation round. This is the overall proposed structure and timeline for the competition.",
