    "details": "<p><strong>1. Competition Launch &amp; Registrations (21st&ndash;27th November)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The competition will officially be launched on 21st November.</li>\n<li>Registrations will remain open until 27th November, 11:50 PM.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>2. Round 1 &ndash; Online Quiz (28th November&ndash;1st December)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>All registered teams will participate in an online quiz round.</li>\n<li>The quiz round will remain open for four days, from 28th November to 1st December.</li>\n<li>The quiz submissions will then be evaluated, and shortlisted teams will qualify for the next round.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>3. Round 2 &ndash; Case Study Submission (3rd&ndash;10th December)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shortlisted teams will receive a case study on 3rd December.</li>\n<li>Teams will have until 10th December, 11:59 PM, to analyse the case and submit their solutions.</li>\n<li>The submission will be in the form of an executive summary presented through a PowerPoint deck.</li>\n<li>The submissions will undergo a two-day evaluation process to shortlist the finalists.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>4. Round 3 &ndash; Final Jury Presentation (14th&ndash;15th December)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The shortlisted finalists will present their case solutions before the jury on 14th and 15th December.</li>\n<li>The jury will evaluate the presentations, assess the proposed solutions, and determine the winners.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Jury &amp; Evaluation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>We are planning to have two jury members from Product Folks, who will evaluate the finalist teams during the final presentation round.</li>\n<li>This is the overall proposed structure and timeline for the competition.</li>\n</ul>",
